{%- doc -%}
  Variant picker for the sk2 product page.

  Stands in for Prestige's `snippets/variant-picker.liquid`, which `sk2-product`
  was written against. Rather than porting that snippet and its `option-value` /
  `select` / `icon` dependency chain, this renders Horizon's own
  `variant-main-picker` — so variant resolution, availability, swatches and the
  URL/section-rendering behaviour are all the theme's real machinery.

  The class names differ between the two themes; `assets/sk2-horizon-bridge.css`
  re-applies the sk2 skin to Horizon's names, so `assets/sk2-home.css` stays
  byte-identical to the source.

  `sk2-product.liquid` also passes `form_id`, `context`, `selector_style`,
  `swatch_selector_style` and `hide_sold_out_variants`. Those are Prestige-only
  concepts — Horizon's picker owns the form wiring itself and drives swatch
  style from Theme settings > Swatches. Liquid ignores unknown render arguments,
  so the call site needs no edit beyond the snippet name.

  @param {object} product - The product to render options for.
  @param {object} [size_chart_page] - Page linked under the options.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign variant_product = product
  if variant_product == blank
    assign variant_product = closest.product
  endif
-%}

{%- unless variant_product == blank or variant_product.has_only_default_variant -%}
  <div class="sk2-variant-picker" data-sk2-variant-picker>
    {%- render 'variant-main-picker',
      product_resource: variant_product,
      section: section,
      product: variant_product
    -%}

    {%- if size_chart_page != blank and size_chart_page.url != blank -%}
      <p class="opt__hint">
        <a href="{{ size_chart_page.url }}">{{ size_chart_page.title }}</a>
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endunless -%}
